{"slug":"cheapest-deletions-to-equal","title":"Make Two Words Equal by Deleting the Cheapest Letters","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":757,"tags":["dp","string","lcs-variant","weighted"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"The letters you keep form a common subsequence; maximise its weight","body":["Delete letters from the word `a` and from the word `b` (any letters, anywhere) until the two words are **equal**. Deleting a letter costs its **ASCII code** (`a` = 97, `b` = 98, ..., `z` = 122). What is the smallest total cost? For `sea` and `eat` the best is to delete `s` from the first word (115) and `t` from the second (116): total 231, and both words become `ea`.","The letters that are **not** deleted form the same word in both, so they form a **common subsequence**. The cost of the deletions is the total weight of all letters of both words minus the weight of the kept letters, counted in both words: `cost = weight(a) + weight(b) - 2 * weight(kept)`. So the task is to find the **common subsequence of the largest weight**. The LCS table works with weights: when the last letters are equal, add the **weight of the letter** instead of 1: `w(i, j) = w(i - 1, j - 1) + code(a[i])`, otherwise `max(w(i - 1, j), w(i, j - 1))`.",{"code":"prev = [0] * (m + 1)\nfor i in range(n):\n    cur = [0] * (m + 1)\n    for j in range(m):\n        if a[i] == b[j]:\n            cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + ord(a[i])\n        else:\n            cur[j + 1] = max(cur[j], prev[j + 1])\n    prev = cur\nprint(sum(map(ord, a)) + sum(map(ord, b)) - 2 * prev[m])"},"Turning a \"delete the cheapest\" question into \"keep the most valuable common part\" is a typical DP move. The time is O(|a| * |b|), at most a million steps, and the memory O(|b|). The answer can be as large as about 240 000, which fits a normal integer."]},"statement":["Two words `a` and `b` are given. You may delete letters from either word; deleting a letter costs its ASCII code (a = 97, ..., z = 122). Print the smallest total cost after which the two words are equal (they may both become empty)."],"inputFormat":["The first line has the word `a`.","The second line has the word `b`."],"outputFormat":["Print the smallest total cost."],"constraints":["1 <= length of a, length of b <= 1000","Both words consist of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"sea\neat\n","output":"231\n","note":"Delete s (115) and t (116): the words become ea. Total 231."},{"input":"abc\nabc\n","output":"0\n","note":"The words are equal already: 0."}],"hints":["The letters that stay form a common subsequence of both words.","The cost is weight(a) + weight(b) - 2 * weight(the kept subsequence).","Use the LCS table, adding the ASCII code of the letter when two letters match."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\na = input().strip()\nb = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string a;\n    cin >> a;\n    string b;\n    cin >> b;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String a = next();\n        String b = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["The kept letters form a common subsequence, so the cost is weight(a) + weight(b) - 2 * the largest weight of a common subsequence; the LCS table is filled with the ASCII code of the letter added when two letters match."],"complexity":"Time O(|a| * |b|), space O(|b|).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\na = input().strip()\nb = input().strip()\n\nn = len(a)\nm = len(b)\nprev = [0] * (m + 1)\nfor i in range(n):\n    cur = [0] * (m + 1)\n    ai = a[i]\n    w = ord(ai)\n    for j in range(m):\n        if b[j] == ai:\n            cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + w\n        else:\n            cur[j + 1] = cur[j] if cur[j] > prev[j + 1] else prev[j + 1]\n    prev = cur\nprint(sum(map(ord, a)) + sum(map(ord, b)) - 2 * prev[m])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string a;\n    cin >> a;\n    string b;\n    cin >> b;\n\n    int n = (int)a.size(), m = (int)b.size();\n    vector<long long> prev(m + 1, 0), cur(m + 1, 0);\n    long long total = 0;\n    for (char ch : a) total += ch;\n    for (char ch : b) total += ch;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n            if (a[i] == b[j]) cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + a[i];\n            else cur[j + 1] = max(cur[j], prev[j + 1]);\n        }\n        swap(prev, cur);\n    }\n    cout << total - 2 * prev[m] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String a = next();\n        String b = next();\n\n        int n = a.length(), m = b.length();\n        long[] prev = new long[m + 1];\n        long[] cur = new long[m + 1];\n        long total = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) total += a.charAt(i);\n        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) total += b.charAt(j);\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n                if (a.charAt(i) == b.charAt(j)) cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + a.charAt(i);\n                else cur[j + 1] = Math.max(cur[j], prev[j + 1]);\n            }\n            long[] swap = prev;\n            prev = cur;\n            cur = swap;\n        }\n        System.out.println(total - 2 * prev[m]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"sea\neat\n","output":"231\n"},{"input":"abc\nabc\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"a\nb\n","output":"195\n"},{"input":"a\na\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"delete\nleet\n","output":"403\n"},{"input":"bababbaabaaababaabba\nbabababaabaababbaabbaabbb\n","output":"683\n"},{"input":"babbabcbbcbcbbaabccbaccbcbcbcbcbababcabbcacbaaaaacbbacbbbacbbbcabaacccbccaaacaabccbcbabbcbbbcbcbccac\nbbbaacbabcbcccabcbbbcbcbaaacabaababccaaacaccbcbbacacccbcaaaccccabbbaaaaaccaccaaaacaaababaacabccbaacb\n","output":"6450\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"25563\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"26460\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"148400\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"37950\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"55750\n"},{"input":"b\\n","output":"97398\n"},{"input":"\nb\n","output":"97368\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"19400\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"219000\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"194\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"97630\n"}]}